  "id": "COMPOUND:33929 - PROTEIN:3745",
  "verbalization": "Donnaienin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the Melanocyte-stimulating hormone receptor through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Donnaienin acts as a target for the enzyme Dihydrofolate reductase (dfrB), which in turn is targeted by a specific compound, (3aR,5aR,8aR,9aR)-1,5,8-trimethylidene-3a,4,5a,6,7,8a,9,9a-octahydroazuleno[6,5-b]furan-2-one. This compound is known to target the Melanocyte-stimulating hormone receptor, indicating a potential mechanism of action through a series of enzymatic and receptor-mediated pathways. The integration of these targets highlights a possible role for Donnaienin in modulating signaling cascades that ultimately influence the activity of the Melanocyte-stimulating hormone receptor. The evidence supports a chain of interactions that links Donnaienin to the receptor through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a complex regulatory mechanism that may be relevant in the context of melanocyte function and signaling.",
